    <bpmn:process id="W_W4700" name="W4700. Mobility Governance, Vendor (Relocation/Immigration Agent) Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor selection/renewal; TPRM (VS-161); performance issue
Frequency: Per vendor + ongoing
Volume: ~6–10 mobility vendors (immigration agents, relocation firms, tax-equalization providers, assignment-payroll vendors)
Owner: Head of Global Mobility
Participants: Procurement (VS-34), TPRM (VS-161), Legal (VS-100.3), Finance (VS-17)
Source: workflow W4700 — Mobility Governance, Vendor (Relocation/Immigration Agent) Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4700_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4700_Lane1" name="Global Mobility">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4700_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4700_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4700_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4700_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4700_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4700_Start3" name="Vendor selection/renewal; TPRM (VS-161); performance issue">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4700_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4700_Task4" name="Select and contract mobility vendors (immigration agents, relocation firms…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Select and contract mobility vendors (immigration agents, relocation firms, tax-equalization/assignment-payroll providers) via procurement (VS-34) and TPRM due diligence (VS-161): licensure, data-security (assignee PII VS-91), conflicts
Responsible (R): Global Mobility / Procurement / TPRM
Accountable (A): Head of Global Mobility / CFO
Duration: Per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4700_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4700_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4700_Task5" name="Govern vendor performance (immigration success rate, relocation SLA, payroll…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Govern vendor performance (immigration success rate, relocation SLA, payroll accuracy); manage the lifecycle (renewal/exit VS-67/VS-161); enforce data-protection agreements (assignee data is sensitive PII VS-91)
Responsible (R): Global Mobility / Vendor Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Global Mobility
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4700_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4700_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
