    <bpmn:process id="W_W4704" name="W4704. Cross-Border Assignment Security &amp; Travel-Risk Linkage" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Cross-border assignment start; travel-risk event
Frequency: Per assignment + on event
Volume: ~15–25 foreign assignees traveling to/from PH (per W4705); sourcing secondees per VS-122
Owner: Head of Global Mobility / Director, Regional Loss Prevention
Participants: Chief Security Officer (VS-159), Travel Risk (VS-159 W4679), OH (VS-83), HR (VS-19)
Source: workflow W4704 — Cross-Border Assignment Security &amp; Travel-Risk Linkage</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4704_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4704_Lane1" name="Global Mobility">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4704_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4704_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4704_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4704_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4704_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4704_Start3" name="Cross-border assignment start; travel-risk event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4704_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4704_Task4" name="For each cross-border assignee, coordinate with Corporate Security (VS-159) on…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: For each cross-border assignee, coordinate with Corporate Security (VS-159) on travel-risk briefing, destination-risk intelligence (VS-159 W4679), and duty-of-care during assignment travel
Responsible (R): Global Mobility / Chief Security Officer / Travel Risk
Accountable (A): Head of Global Mobility / Chief Security Officer
Duration: Per assignment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4704_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4704_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4704_Task5" name="Ensure assignees are enrolled in traveler-tracking and emergency protocols…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Ensure assignees are enrolled in traveler-tracking and emergency protocols (VS-159 W4687/W4688); coordinate medical-evacuation and security support for high-risk locations
Responsible (R): Global Mobility / Chief Security Officer / OH
Accountable (A): Head of Global Mobility / Chief Security Officer
Duration: Per assignment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4704_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4704_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4704_Task6" name="On a security/travel-risk event affecting an assignee, activate the VS-159…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: On a security/travel-risk event affecting an assignee, activate the VS-159 response and support the assignee/family; feed lessons into mobility-risk (W4703)
Responsible (R): Global Mobility / Chief Security Officer
Accountable (A): Head of Global Mobility / Chief Security Officer
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4704_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4704_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4704_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4704_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4704_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-130 (ensure immigration &amp; foreign-worker compliance.) | - CTL-710: cross-border assignees briefed + tracked (VS-159); duty-of-care discharged; joint response on event
Owner: Head of Global Mobility / Director, Regional Loss Prevention</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
